cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use open-cake-ir, cite this software and identify the source revision and workload used."
type: software
title: "open-cake-ir: Agent-driven compiler and kernel co-evolution"
authors:
  - family-names: "Qin"
    given-names: "Haiyan"
    email: "haiyanq@buaa.edu.cn"
    affiliation: "Beihang University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/qhy991/open-cake-ir"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A research system for agent-driven co-evolution of GPU kernels and compiler
  capabilities. Agents author kernels through a structured execution plan, use
  compiler and on-device feedback, and improve the compiler when real workloads
  expose representation, verification, lowering, or analysis gaps. Source identity
  is the git commit of the checkout, so a citation should name the commit the work
  was run at along with the target and workload.
keywords:
  - GPU kernels
  - compilers
  - intermediate representation
  - agent systems
  - CUDA
  - Metal
  - HIP
